The {{nihongo|'''Kanemoto clan'''|金本氏|Kanemoto-shi}} was a [[Sanese clan|Sanese samurai clan]] and dynasty which established [[Kanemoto Shogunate]] and ruled the southern court ([[Nakamizu]]) between 1336 to 1604 where they lost [[Fushimi Castle]] to [[Kawaei Clan]] during [[Siege of Fushimi (1604)]] and subsequently thrown to rule [[Aoyama Domain|Aoyama]] under Kawaei Shogunate. Kanemoto clan descended from branch of [[Mononobe clan]] from the town of [[Fushimi, Miyagami|Fushimi]] in [[Miyagami Prefecture|Miyagami]].

The clan initially overshadowed by larger [[Kurokoma clan]] of Nakamizu until the [[Kurokoma-Kanemoto War]] in 1337 over the complete control of what was the southern [[Miyagi Empire]] where Kanemoto become victorious with the favor from being protectors of the imperial line and established [[Kanemoto Shogunate]] with [[Kanemoto Masatsune]] as the first Kanemoto Shogun.

